            <ArticleTitle>The role of radioisotopic methods in imaging of intervertebral disc inflammation in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present the case of a 17-year-old girl, with pain over lumbar spine area, treated by paediatricians and rehabilitation specialists, discussing diagnostic imaging and laboratory examinations together with clinical observations. Spondylodiscitis was diagnosed after bone scintigraphy with 99mTc-MDP, the course of disease was monitored by immunoscintigraphy amongst other techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
